From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:14:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: renderer, window and build switch

Ties the Dolby Vision pieces into VideoPlayer and the GBM window, and
adds the build switch:

- Eligibility (DVPlaybackPolicy.h): a stream takes the native path when
  the display takes Standard Dolby Vision, the tunnel is available and
  the source is Dolby Vision (or HDR10+ to convert), not a software
  probe, interlaced or stereo; a picture also has to be a decoded VAAPI
  surface, so software-decoded pictures play through the ordinary
  renderer (HDR10 for a compatible base layer).
- VideoPlayer and CRenderManager: a refresh-rate switch for a native
  stream is left for the bridge's first commit (one HDMI change), the
  stream's native rate is kept until its first picture, the startup and
  end-of-stream waits use CDVPrivateDrain, and overlays are reported to
  the window.
- CLinuxRendererGLES and CRendererVAAPIGLES: a native picture goes to
  the engine before any GL texture is made (no vaExportSurfaceHandle
  texture, vaSyncSurface, EGL images or YUV shaders), and every queued
  picture is numbered so that a repeat can be recognised.
- CWinSystemGbmGLESContext: BeginDVBridge and EndDVBridge (signal up in
  the selected output mode, restore of the ordinary display, retried
  when refused), the black Dolby Vision startup signal before playback
  is released, the menu output (the GUI packed by dvbridge_gl_pack with
  graphics-only metadata), the GUI framebuffer shared with the engine
  (half resolution and reuse on request), PresentRender committing the
  engine's buffers (a held repeat waits for the next vertical blank;
  with DV_PRIVATE_NONBLOCK=1 flips are queued and
  GetFrameLatencyAdjustment adds the refresh), display resets and
  modesets during output, and HDR10 and HDR10+ through the tunnel with a
  notification when the connection refuses them. The menu target is
  recreated after a menu return, and a pass that commits nothing pauses
  10 ms instead of spinning.
- Build: option(ENABLE_DVBRIDGE) in the top-level CMakeLists.txt defines
  HAVE_DVBRIDGE for every target, since the headers change class
  layouts; VideoRenderers builds tools/dvbridge and the adapter, and the
  targets that call them link dvbridge_core. The LibreELEC recipe turns
  it on only for x86_64 Generic with GBM, OpenGL ES and Vulkan.

Needs every patch before it in yblod-engine/patches/kodi/. Until this
one, ENABLE_DVBRIDGE does not exist and the guarded code is compiled
out; the intermediate states are not build-tested, the series as a
whole is. Queued flips (DV_PRIVATE_NONBLOCK=1) could not be tested
without a display and ship off.

Formerly the renderer, window and build parts of kodi-9990-native-dv,
with kodi-9994-hdmi-recovery, kodi-9995-diagnostics and
kodi-9996-output-modes-and-info (their window parts),
kodi-9999-dv-display-reset, kodi-9999-dv-single-modeset, yblod-01 to
-07, -10 (live display coordination), -15, -21 to -25, -29 to -31, -34,
-35 (even geometry), -40 to -49 (0.5.0 presentation rework), -58, -59
and -61.
